Evaluation Mapping Examples
The public sample may illustrate potential mappings to evaluation workflows.
These mappings are illustrative only. They do not constitute complete evaluation suites, standardized RAG test sets, production-ready input/output datasets, fully defined retrieval-context structures, or framework-specific benchmark formats.
Retrieval quality
An aligned regulatory segment may be used as a reference unit when examining whether a system retrieves a relevant legal or regulatory passage.
Source grounding
CELEX identifiers, structural references and EUR-Lex URLs may support review of whether an output remains traceable to official EU legal sources.
Faithfulness
A generated, summarized or transformed output may be compared with the source regulatory segment to assess whether meaning has been preserved.
Cross-language consistency
Aligned language versions may support review of whether regulatory meaning remains consistent across language versions.
Translation fidelity
Aligned official language versions may support evaluation workflows involving legal/regulatory translation fidelity, terminology consistency and preservation of regulatory meaning.
Regulatory QA
Structured segments and source traceability may support workflows involving legal and regulatory information quality assessment.
Important limitation
THT Legal Data is not a legal AI application, legal assistant, compliance platform, legal reasoning benchmark, hallucination benchmark, RAG benchmark or agent benchmark.
The benchmark may support evaluation workflows involving retrieval, grounding, faithfulness, translation fidelity and cross-language consistency, but this repository does not provide complete evaluation suites or framework-specific benchmark formats.
